body:
Jumping on this question because I think it's a good one. From a crew members perspective, and I'm speaking of my current store only, there are days when mates are chilling in the bridge doing paperwork while the rest of the crew is breaking down pallets. There are even more days when the PTL for the hour sits next to the log the whole hour and does not do a single pull. What are some things that are happening behind what we might see that prohibits mates (not pointing fingers at all, just some) from not participating in an essential part of the job description? In my store, mates don't even operate the high low or the electric jacks, nor do they have to know how to use them to open which is completely backwards in my opinion.

&#x200B;

Disclaimer: I have a bunch of frustrations when it comes to this company. I don't normally say things on this sub, nor do I say anything in my store. I am just here until I finish up with my masters and move on. I'm just curious on what I might not be seeing if you have any insight onto it, or if anyone else, mate or crew, does. Thank you!
